From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 05:39:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] Priority 2 UX: reps quick-add, RPE/Tempo dropdowns,
 Home dashboard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#5 Reps quick-add: +1/+2/+5 (and -1) buttons in the set dialog, alongside
   the existing weight quick-add.
#7 RPE: replaced free-text entry with labelled preset chips
   (RPE 6 Easy ... RPE 10 Failure, plus 'No RPE'). Stored as the same
   SetLog.rpe Double.
#6 Tempo: replaced raw notation entry with named presets (Normal 2-0-2,
   Controlled 3-1-2, Slow Eccentric 4-1-2, Pause Reps 3-2-1, Custom,
   Not tracked) that translate to notation behind the scenes; Custom keeps
   a manual field. Stored as the same SetLog.tempo String.
   New pure helper: domain/logging/SetInputPresets.kt.
#3 Home vs Workout separation: Home is now a dashboard — today's
   recommendation + recovery (Smart Coach card), weekly progress
   (sessions + volume this week), day streak, total workouts, coaching
   insight and last PR; removed the duplicate Start Workout button and the
   recent-workouts feed (those belong to the Workout/History tabs).
   New pure helper: domain/home/HomeDashboardStats.kt (weekly progress +
   day-streak), wired into HomeViewModel.

Compile-safe and additive: storage model unchanged (rpe Double?, tempo
String?); all set-save signatures unchanged. New pure-Kotlin helpers
type-check on kotlinc 1.9.22 and pass logic tests (RPE/Tempo: 3, streak/
weekly: 5) run in-sandbox. No tests committed (kept build/CI test-free).
